            <ArticleTitle>Isolated obturator externus muscle abscess presenting as hip pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>137-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The case of a 20-year-old diabetic male with 2 weeks of hip pain, diagnosed with an isolated obturator externus muscle abscess, is reported. Pyomyositis, or abscess formation deep within a large striated muscle, is a rare but potentially life-threatening disease.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
